WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:01.395
The heart of the wreck.

00:02.095 --> 00:11.724
At the centre is what remains of the star's core: a ball about twenty kilometres across with the mass of a sun, spinning thirty times a second.

00:12.174 --> 00:14.054
It is called a pulsar.

00:14.504 --> 00:19.076
It is far too small to see, but the blue glow in the middle is its doing.

00:19.526 --> 00:22.399
An even heavier star leaves a black hole.
